{"name":"Bowling Green","hex":"#bfdeaf","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bowling Green","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States:\nA city in Hardee County, Florida.\nAn unincorporated community in Clay County, Indiana.\nA home rule city, the county seat of Warren County, Kentucky.\n\nAn unincorporated community and census-designated place in Allegany County, Maryland.\nA city, the county seat of Pike County, Missouri.\nA city, the county seat of Wood County, Ohio.\nAn unincorporated community in Delaware County, Pennsylvania.\nAn incorporated town, the county seat of Caroline County, Virginia.","A city in Hardee County, Florida."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bowling_Green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bowling Green, Kentucky","blocks":[{"text":"Bowling Green is a city in and the county seat of Warren County, Kentucky, United States. Its population was 72,294 as of the 2020 census, making it the third-most populous city in the state, after Louisville and Lexington. The Bowling Green metropolitan area is the fourth-largest in the state and had a population of 179,639 in 2020."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Fountain_Square_Park%2C_Bowling_Green%2C_Kentucky.JPG/330px-Fountain_Square_Park%2C_Bowling_Green%2C_Kentucky.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bowling_Green%2C_Kentucky","wikidata":"Q694545"},{"title":"Bowling Green metropolitan area, Kentucky","blocks":[{"text":"The Bowling Green Metropolitan Statistical Area, as defined by the United States Census Bureau, is an area consisting of four counties in Kentucky, anchored by the city of Bowling Green. As of 2014, the MSA had an estimated population of 165,732."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Fountain_Square_Park%2C_Bowling_Green%2C_Kentucky.JPG/330px-Fountain_Square_Park%2C_Bowling_Green%2C_Kentucky.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bowling_Green_metropolitan_area%2C_Kentucky","wikidata":"Q4951176"},{"title":"Bowling green","blocks":[{"text":"A bowling green is a finely laid, close-mown and rolled stretch of turf for playing the game of bowls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Bowling_green-KayEss-1.jpeg/330px-Bowling_green-KayEss-1.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bowling_green","wikidata":"Q895453"},{"title":"Bowling","blocks":[{"text":"Bowling is a target sport and recreational activity in which a player rolls a ball toward pins or another target. Most references to bowling are to pin bowling, specifically tenpin bowling. Bowling can also refer to target bowling, such as lawn bowls. Bowling is played by 120 million people in more than 90 countries, including 70 million people in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/US_Navy_090819-N-2259V-119_A_Sailor_releases_the_ball_down_the_lane_at_a_bowling_competition_during_the_2009_San_Diego_Surface_Line_Week.jpg/330px-US_Navy_090819-N-2259V-119_A_Sailor_releases_the_ball_down_the_lane_at_a_bowling_competition_during_the_2009_San_Diego_Surface_Line_Week.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bowling","wikidata":"Q3177899"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/ReservoirHill.jpg/500px-ReservoirHill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/ReservoirHill.jpg/1280px-ReservoirHill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/ReservoirHill.jpg/500px-ReservoirHill.jpg?utm_sou